Build x86 MMX/SSE* code per function with target attributes instead of
global -mmmx/-msse*, which let the compiler use cmov, SSE, etc. in all
generic code, breaking the i586 baseline. The SIMD code paths are still
selected by the existing runtime CPUID detection, and SSE2/SSE3 are now
also available on i586 builds.

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

